0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the 6502 (NMOS opcodes only)
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-24). -n? does no more editing than
0000                             ;        Backspace. Ctrl-C stops every build (see the console layer); the
0000                             ;        break-off cell is BRKOFF, $047B.
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter; see b8s-z80.asm for the common ideas.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  This interpreter keeps the data stack in pages 2 and 3 (252 cells) and
0000                             ;  uses 10 bytes of zero page ($00-$09). b8s-6502-zp.asm is a smaller interpreter that
0000                             ;  keeps the stack in zero page instead (112 cells); its memory map and
0000                             ;  machine-code contract differ.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks: whatever the spec calls unsafe is not caught
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build, as in the spec's "Errors and checked
0000                             ;                 builds": at startup every word cell points at 0000h (see
0000                             ;                 e_undef) and the variables and the interpreter's cells are
0000                             ;                 0. It stops with S s R r (stack over/underflow), H (heap),
0000                             ;                 O (a store outside the program's space), U (undefined
0000                             ;                 word), Q (no closing quote), W (bad character after [), X
0000                             ;                 (a reserved byte), Z (divide by zero), N (brackets) or B
0000                             ;                 (Ctrl-C), printing the spec's four-line report:
0000                             ;                   Err Z @ 3,4
0000                             ;                   0/ "no"$
0000                             ;                   Stk 2: 5 0
0000                             ;                   Rtn 0
0000                             ;                 and then goes to EXIT.
0000                             ;    ANSI     what the console escapes of "$" (/00bbIC8= /| /` /~) do:
0000                             ;             1 = send ANSI (VT100) sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = call the machine's own routines CONCLS, CONEOL, CONCUR and
0000                             ;                 CONAT (see the equates)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, C6502 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                ANSI:     EQU   0   ; 1 = the console escapes send ANSI sequences
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Registers and zero page
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    IP      zero-page pointer to the next program character (16 bits)
0000                             ;    TL/TH   the top data-stack cell (TOS) lives in zero page, not in memory
0000                             ;    X       data-stack index. The stack is two byte-planes, grows down, and
0000                             ;            holds everything under TOS: NOS is DSL,X (low) and DSH,X (high).
0000                             ;            The stack never leaves its planes because X is 8 bits.
0000                             ;    S       the hardware stack is the RETURN stack: a word call or "(" pushes
0000                             ;            the reading position (high byte first, then low) and "]" or ")"
0000                             ;            pulls it. 100 entries (200 bytes) fit with room to spare.
0000                             ;    Y, A    scratch. Y is 0 after peek/getc, and the zero-page indirect reads
0000                             ;            (IP),Y rely on that.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch: step is called with JSR, so a handler ends with a plain RTS and
0000                             ;  lands on "JMP next" in the loop. Punctuation goes through PTAB with the
0000                             ;  RTS trick (push handler-1, RTS). Handlers that use the return stack ( ( ) \
0000                             ;  ] 00bbIA== and word calls ) first pull the 2-byte JSR frame off (PLA PLA) and end
0000                             ;  with JMP next instead.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Every punctuation handler starts with the carry clear (the range sort in
0000                             ;  step leaves it so). Several of them count on that, where the comments say.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Machine-code contract (the grave): the code at TOS is entered as a
0000                             ;  subroutine, by JMP (T0) with the loop's return address on the hardware
0000                             ;  stack, so it ends with RTS (60h, which the hex loader appends). On entry
0000                             ;  TL/TH ($02/$03) hold the new TOS (the address is already consumed) and X is
0000                             ;  the data-stack index: NOS is DSL,X (low) and DSH,X (high), which is
0000                             ;  $0200,X and $0300,X.
0000                             ;  To push: DEX, store TL/TH at DSL,X/DSH,X, then set TL/TH. To drop: load
0000                             ;  TL/TH from DSL,X/DSH,X and INX. The code may change A, Y, X (it is the
0000                             ;  stack index, so it must stay consistent on return) and zero page $04-$06
0000                             ;  and $08-$09; it must keep IP ($00/$01) and the hardware stack balanced. On
0000                             ;  return TL/TH are the TOS. Zero page $0A-$0F is free for the code's own use.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                IP:       EQU   00h   ; 00-01 reading position
0000                TL:       EQU   02h   ; TOS low
0000                TH:       EQU   03h   ; TOS high
0000                T0:       EQU   04h   ; scratch
0000                T1:       EQU   05h   
0000                T2:       EQU   06h   
0000                D0:       EQU   08h   ; divisor (division, number printing)
0000                D1:       EQU   09h   
0000                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    KEYBUF:   EQU   07h   ; a key held back by the break check (0: none)
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CHECKED   
0000                PLACE:    EQU   06h   ; 06-07 (T2 and $07) the address of the
0000                             ;   character being run, for the error report:
0000                             ;   no handler of the checked build uses T2.
0000                             ;   (Machine code may change T2: that matters
0000                             ;   only if it also leaves a stack overrun,
0000                             ;   whose report then shows a wrong place.)
0000                RSV:      EQU   LET+35h   ; S as it was before this character
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; a key held back by the break check (0: none)
0000                             ; The error report runs after the program, so it may use the zero page that
0000                             ; machine code has ($0A-$0F):
0000                CL:       EQU   0Ah   ; 0A-0B the column being reported
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    0000-00FF  zero page: the variables above
0000                             ;    0100-01FF  hardware stack = return stack, S starts at FF
0000                             ;    0200       DSL, data stack, low bytes (X = FC when empty: 252 cells)
0000                             ;    0300       DSH, data stack, high bytes
0000                             ;    0400       LET  letter cells: A..Z at +00..+33, a..z at +40..+73 (a word
0000                             ;               cell is 64 bytes below its variable), heap pointer at +7C,
0000                             ;               the -n? line buffer at +80..+FF. The checked build's cells
0000                             ;               are in the gaps: RSV at +35, PEND at +38, KEYBUF (the held
0000                             ;               key; $07 in the unchecked build) at +7A; and every build's:
0000                             ;               CDOWN at +79, BRKOFF (the break-off cell) at +7B.
0000                             ;    0500       PROG the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap follows
0000                             ;    E000       the interpreter (ROM)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the page range LETPAGE..HEAPLIM-1.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (it does
0000                             ;   if the routine ends with LDA / RTS).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve X and Y.
0000                          IF   1-ANSI   
0000                             ; With ANSI = 0 the console escapes of "$" call these. All four must keep X;
0000                             ; they may change A, Y and the flags.
0000                CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Ch   ; /{  clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
0000                CONEOL:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; /}  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
0000                CONCUR:   EQU   0FF12h   ; /| and /`  show the cursor if the carry is set,
0000                             ;     hide it if the carry is clear
0000                CONAT:    EQU   0FF15h   ; /~  the cursor to row A, column Y, both
0000                             ;     counted from 0
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                DSL:      EQU   0200h   ; data stack, low bytes
0000                DSH:      EQU   0300h   ; data stack, high bytes
0000                DSE:      EQU   0FCh   ; X when the data stack is empty
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   04h   
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                PROG:     EQU   0500h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                PROG1:    EQU   PROG+1   
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0E0h   ; the heap must stay below E000h (a page)
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer (the heap top)
0000                CDOWN:    EQU   LET+79h   ; the break check's countdown (see pnext)
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ; the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                PEND:     EQU   LET+38h   ; checked: the program's end, where the heap
0000                             ;   starts: it may not be released below it
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   20h   ; lowest S allowed (checked build)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ;   (each pass calls KEY once; the wait for a
0000                             ;   second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms)
0000                CWAIT:    EQU   250*MSLOOP/256   ; (that wait, in 256s)
E000                          .ORG   0E000h   
E000                             ; =============================================================================
E000                             ;  Startup: find the NUL, the heap starts after it
E000                             ; =============================================================================
E000   A2 FF        START:    LDX   #0FFh   
E002   9A                     TXS      ; return stack empty
E003                          IF   CHECKED   
E003                             ; The first half of the letter page is zeroed: every variable, every
E003                             ; cell of the interpreter's own (no key held back), and every word
E003                             ; cell, which then points at 0000h: calling an undefined word stops
E003                             ; with U (see e_undef).
E003   E8                     INX      
E004   8A                     TXA      ; A = 0
E005   A0 7F                  LDY   #7Fh   
E007   99 00 04     STZ:      STA   LET,Y   
E00A   88                     DEY      
E00B   10 FA                  BPL   stz   
E00D                          ENDIF      
E00D   20 96 E3               JSR   rstip   
E010   20 8A E3     ST1:      JSR   getc   
E013   D0 FB                  BNE   st1   ; IP ends just past the NUL
E015                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              STA   KEYBUF   ; (A = 0) no key held, the break key on
                              STA   BRKOFF   
E015                          ENDIF      
E015   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E017   8D 7C 04               STA   HEAP   
E01A                          IF   CHECKED   
E01A   8D 38 04               STA   PEND   
E01D                          ENDIF      
E01D   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E01F   8D 7D 04               STA   HEAP+1   
E022                          IF   CHECKED   
E022   8D 39 04               STA   PEND+1   
E025                          ENDIF      
E025   20 96 E3               JSR   rstip   
E028   A2 FC                  LDX   #DSE   
E02A                             ; =============================================================================
E02A                             ;  The inner loop
E02A                             ; =============================================================================
E02A                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
E02A                             ;  The break key. A running program reads the keyboard only through getk
E02A                             ;  (for "?") and pnext (the break check), which between them give the break
E02A                             ;  key its rules:
E02A                             ;    - Ctrl-C (03h) stops the program: silently to EXIT in the unchecked
E02A                             ;      build, with the report (B) in the checked one;
E02A                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
E02A                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
E02A                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
E02A                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
E02A                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
E02A                             ;  KEY is the host's: a waiting key in A, or A = 0 with the zero flag set.
E02A                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
E02A                             ; pnext: the break check, then (falling through) next. A word call, a true
E02A                             ; "(" and a true ")" end here, but the keyboard is looked at only once in 256
E02A                             ; of them: CDOWN counts them down. A key found is held; a Ctrl-C goes on to ctlc. (Startup
E02A                             ; falls in here too, which does no harm.)
E02A   CE 79 04     PNEXT:    DEC   CDOWN   
E02D   D0 0B                  BNE   next   
E02F   20 06 FF               JSR   KEY   
E032   F0 06                  BEQ   next   ; no key
E034   8D 7A 04               STA   KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
E037   20 CC E0               JSR   chk3   ; (Ctrl-C: back only if the break key is off)
E03A                NEXT:        
E03A                          IF   CHECKED   
E03A                             ; Both stacks are checked once per character, after it has run. The
E03A                             ; return stack has overrun when S is below RSLIM: an overflow leaves
E03A                             ; it at 1Eh or 1Fh, an underflow wraps it to 01h (no handler pulls
E03A                             ; more than one entry). The data stack has when X is above DSE: an
E03A                             ; underflow moves X up to FDh or FEh (no handler moves X by more
E03A                             ; than 2, but "$", whose /~ escapes each look first), and an
E03A                             ; overflow wraps it from 00h to FFh.
E03A                             ; S is kept in RSV, for the report's Rtn line (an error found inside
E03A                             ; a handler has its own calls on the hardware stack), and the place
E03A                             ; of the character about to run in PLACE.
E03A   8A                     TXA      ; TSX trashes X: keep it in A
E03B   BA                     TSX      
E03C   8E 35 04               STX   RSV   
E03F   E0 20                  CPX   #RSLIM   
E041   AA                     TAX      ; TAX leaves the carry alone
E042   90 12                  BCC   e_rstack   
E044   E0 FD                  CPX   #DSE+1   
E046   B0 20                  BCS   e_stack   
E048   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E04A   85 06                  STA   PLACE   
E04C   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E04E   85 07                  STA   PLACE+1   
E050                          ENDIF      
E050   20 12 E1               JSR   step   
E053   4C 3A E0               JMP   next   
E056                          IF   CHECKED   
E056                             ; S/R are overflows, s/r underflows. After an underflow that stack counts as
E056                             ; empty.
E056   AD 35 04     E_RSTACK:   LDA   RSV   
E059   C9 10                  CMP   #10h   
E05B   A9 52                  LDA   #"R"   
E05D   B0 13                  BCS   ejmp   ; S is 1Eh-1Fh: an overflow
E05F   A9 FF                  LDA   #0FFh   
E061   8D 35 04               STA   RSV   ; S wrapped to 01h: Rtn 0
E064   A9 72                  LDA   #"r"   
E066   D0 0A                  BNE   ejmp   ; always
E068   E0 FF        E_STACK:   CPX   #0FFh   
E06A   A9 53                  LDA   #"S"   
E06C   B0 04                  BCS   ejmp   ; X wrapped from 00h to FFh: an overflow
E06E   A2 FC                  LDX   #DSE   ; an underflow: Stk 0
E070   A9 73                  LDA   #"s"   
E072   4C E5 E5     EJMP:     JMP   error   
E075                          ENDIF      
E075                             ; The handlers that work on the return stack sit here, where short branches
E075                             ; reach next and pnext.
E075                             ; "{" TOS to the return stack, "}" return stack to TOS
E075   68           H_TOR:    PLA      
E076   68                     PLA      
E077   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E079   48                     PHA      
E07A   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E07C   48                     PHA      
E07D   20 C7 E3               JSR   drop   
E080   D0 B8                  BNE   next   ; always
E082   68           H_FROMR:   PLA      
E083   68                     PLA      
E084   20 76 E1               JSR   push   
E087   68                     PLA      
E088   85 02                  STA   TL   
E08A   68                     PLA      
E08B   85 03                  STA   TH   
E08D   90 AB                  BCC   next   ; always: the carry is clear on the way in
E08F                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
E08F                             ; drops it and carries on. It shares "]"s code: with the carry clear, as
E08F                             ; it is here, the address popped is pushed back.
E08F   20 9F E3     H_CLOSE:   JSR   flag   
E092   F0 20                  BEQ   rdrop   
E094   24                     DB   24h   ; (BIT zp: steps over the SEC)
E095                             ; "]" returns: pull an address and jump to it.
E095   38           H_RET:    SEC      
E096   68                     PLA      
E097   68                     PLA      ; drop the step frame
E098   68                     PLA      
E099   85 00                  STA   IP   
E09B   68                     PLA      
E09C   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E09E   B0 9A                  BCS   next   
E0A0   48                     PHA      ; ")": keep the block start
E0A1   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E0A3   48                     PHA      
E0A4   90 84                  BCC   pnext   ; always: a loop-back, with the break check
E0A6                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
E0A6                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns.
E0A6   20 9F E3     H_BREAK:   JSR   flag   
E0A9   F0 25                  BEQ   gk9   ; (an RTS)
E0AB                          IF   CHECKED   
E0AB   A9 00                  LDA   #0   ; \ takes either closer
E0AD                          ENDIF      
E0AD   20 D1 E1               JSR   skip   
E0B0   C9 29                  CMP   #")"   
E0B2   D0 E1                  BNE   h_ret   
E0B4   68           RDROP:    PLA      
E0B5   68                     PLA      
E0B6   68                     PLA      
E0B7   68                     PLA      ; (the block start's high byte: never 0)
E0B8   D0 80                  BNE   next   ; always
E0BA                             ; getk: a key for "?" in A (zero flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag
E0BA                             ; set when there is none. Keeps X and Y. The held key goes first, and is
E0BA                             ; taken out of KEYBUF.
E0BA   AD 7A 04     GETK:     LDA   KEYBUF   
E0BD   F0 08                  BEQ   gk1   
E0BF   48                     PHA      
E0C0   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E0C2   8D 7A 04               STA   KEYBUF   
E0C5   68                     PLA      
E0C6   60                     RTS      
E0C7   20 06 FF     GK1:      JSR   KEY   
E0CA   F0 04                  BEQ   gk9   
E0CC                             ; chk3: a key in A (not 0). A Ctrl-C goes on to ctlc, which gives the 03h
E0CC                             ; back if it comes back at all.
E0CC   C9 03        CHK3:     CMP   #3   
E0CE   F0 01                  BEQ   ctlc   
E0D0   60           GK9:      RTS      
E0D1                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
E0D1                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms (about 250 times MSLOOP
E0D1                             ; looks: D0 counts the 256s, D1 runs on from whatever it holds) for one more
E0D1                             ; key: a second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest
E0D1                             ; wins). Returns A = 03h with the zero flag clear. Keeps X and Y.
E0D1   AD 7B 04     CTLC:     LDA   BRKOFF   
E0D4   F0 1D                  BEQ   cbreak   
E0D6   A9 28                  LDA   #CWAIT+1   
E0D8   85 08                  STA   D0   
E0DA   20 06 FF     CT2:      JSR   KEY   
E0DD   D0 0A                  BNE   ct3   
E0DF   C6 09                  DEC   D1   
E0E1   D0 F7                  BNE   ct2   
E0E3   C6 08                  DEC   D0   
E0E5   D0 F3                  BNE   ct2   
E0E7   F0 07                  BEQ   ct9   ; always: none came
E0E9   C9 03        CT3:      CMP   #3   
E0EB   F0 06                  BEQ   cbreak   
E0ED   8D 7A 04               STA   KEYBUF   
E0F0   A9 03        CT9:      LDA   #3   
E0F2   60                     RTS      
E0F3                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    CBREAK:   EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
E0F3                          ENDIF      
E0F3                          IF   CHECKED   
E0F3                CBREAK:   EQU   e_break   ; the checked build reports B
E0F3                          ENDIF      
E0F3                          IF   CHECKED   
E0F3   A9 42        E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C (the stacks as they stand)
E0F5   2C                     DB   2Ch   
E0F6   A9 58        E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte, 80h-FFh
E0F8   4C E5 E5     EJMP3:    JMP   error   
E0FB                          ENDIF      
E0FB                          IF   CHECKED   
E0FB                             ; e_undef: the word cells of undefined words hold 0000h. A call there reads
E0FB                             ; the byte at 0000h, which is IP's own low byte: 00h while IP is 0000h, so
E0FB                             ; the call reads a NUL with IP in page zero, where no program can be. The
E0FB                             ; call is undone first: the step frame and the return address come off the
E0FB                             ; hardware stack, and the place is the call letter (the return address - 1).
E0FB   68           E_UNDEF:   PLA      
E0FC   68                     PLA      ; the step frame
E0FD   68                     PLA      
E0FE   38                     SEC      
E0FF   E9 01                  SBC   #1   
E101   85 06                  STA   PLACE   
E103   68                     PLA      
E104   E9 00                  SBC   #0   
E106   85 07                  STA   PLACE+1   
E108   EE 35 04               INC   RSV   
E10B   EE 35 04               INC   RSV   ; Rtn does not count the call
E10E   A9 55                  LDA   #"U"   
E110   D0 E6                  BNE   ejmp3   ; always
E112                          ENDIF      
E112                             ; step: read one character and sort it by range.
E112                             ;    00h          end of program
E112                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored
E112                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
E112                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
E112                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
E112                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
E112                             ; Every way out of the sort has the carry clear, except "ignored". A checked
E112                             ; build stops on 80h-FFh (X) and still ignores DEL.
E112   20 8A E3     STEP:     JSR   getc   ; flags follow A
E115   F0 38                  BEQ   endprog   
E117   38                     SEC      
E118   E9 21                  SBC   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
E11A   90 32                  BCC   ign   ; 01h-20h
E11C   C9 0F                  CMP   #0Fh   
E11E   90 24                  BCC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: index 0-14
E120   E9 0F                  SBC   #0Fh   ; (carry set) A = c - 30h
E122   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E124   90 35                  BCC   digit   
E126   C9 11                  CMP   #11h   
E128   90 18                  BCC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
E12A   E9 11                  SBC   #11h   ; (carry set) A = c - 41h
E12C   C9 1A                  CMP   #1Ah   
E12E   90 26                  BCC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah
E130   C9 20                  CMP   #20h   
E132   90 0C                  BCC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
E134   C9 3A                  CMP   #3Ah   
E136   90 2B                  BCC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h
E138   C9 3E                  CMP   #3Eh   
E13A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BCS   ign   ; 7Fh-FFh
E13A                          ENDIF      
E13A                          IF   CHECKED   
E13A   F0 12                  BEQ   ign   ; 7Fh
E13C   B0 B8                  BCS   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
E13E                          ENDIF      
E13E                             ; The three adjustments below chain. Each ADC adds the carry the one
E13E                             ; before it left, which the constants allow for.
E13E   E9 1A                  SBC   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: (carry clear: -1Bh) index 28-31
E140   69 F6        P5B:      ADC   #0F6h   ; 5Bh-60h: -10 (-9 when chained), index 22-27
E142   69 05        P3A:      ADC   #5   ; 3Ah-40h: +5 (+6 when chained), index 15-21
E144   0A           PUNCT:    ASL      ; (the index is small: the carry stays clear)
E145   A8                     TAY      
E146   B9 00 E3               LDA   PTAB+1,Y   
E149   48                     PHA      
E14A   B9 FF E2               LDA   PTAB,Y   
E14D   48                     PHA      
E14E   60           IGN:      RTS      ; RTS trick: goes to the handler. Reached
E14F                             ; directly, it just ends an ignored character.
E14F                ENDPROG:      
E14F                          IF   CHECKED   
E14F   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   ; IP in page zero: an undefined word
E151   F0 A8                  BEQ   e_undef   
E153                          ENDIF      
E153   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   
E156                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
E156                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
E156   0A           UPPER:    ASL      
E157   A8                     TAY      
E158   38                     SEC      
E159   B0 2C                  BCS   pushn   ; always
E15B                             ; Digits: the first one is in A; read the rest of the number.
E15B   A0 00        DIGIT:    LDY   #0   
E15D   20 6C E1               JSR   pushay   
E160   4C 64 E3               JMP   rdnum   
E163                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
E163   0A           LOWER:    ASL      
E164   A0 04                  LDY   #>LET   
E166   D0 04                  BNE   pushay   ; always
E168   A5 00        PUSHIP:   LDA   IP   ; push the reading position
E16A   A4 01                  LDY   IP+1   
E16C                             ; pushay: push a cell: A = its low byte, Y = its high byte
E16C   48           PUSHAY:   PHA      
E16D   20 76 E1               JSR   push   
E170   68                     PLA      
E171   85 02                  STA   TL   
E173   84 03                  STY   TH   
E175   60                     RTS      
E176   CA           PUSH:     DEX      ; ":" and every push (keeps Y)
E177   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E179   9D 00 02               STA   DSL,X   
E17C   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E17E   9D 00 03               STA   DSH,X   
E181   60                     RTS      
E182                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
E182                             ; the matching ")".
E182   20 9F E3     H_OPEN:   JSR   flag   ; (keeps the carry clear)
E185                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BEQ   skip   
E185                          ENDIF      
E185                          IF   CHECKED   
E185   F0 25                  BEQ   skpar   
E187                          ENDIF      
E187                             ; pushn: take the step frame off, push the reading position on the return
E187                             ; stack, and go on. With the carry set (a word call) the reading position
E187                             ; then becomes the address in the letter cell at LET,Y.
E187   68           PUSHN:    PLA      
E188   68                     PLA      ; drop the step frame
E189   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E18B   48                     PHA      
E18C   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E18E   48                     PHA      
E18F   90 0A                  BCC   nxt   
E191   B9 00 04               LDA   LET,Y   
E194   85 00                  STA   IP   
E196   B9 01 04               LDA   LET+1,Y   
E199   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E19B   4C 2A E0     NXT:      JMP   pnext   
E19E                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
E19E                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
E19E                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
E19E                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
E19E                             ; checked build stops on it.)
E19E                          IF   CHECKED   
E19E   C0 DF        DEF1:     CPY   #" "-"A"+256   
E1A0   F0 2A                  BEQ   def2   
E1A2                             ; W: anything but a letter or a space after [. The place is that character,
E1A2                             ; one past the [.
E1A2   E6 06                  INC   PLACE   
E1A4   D0 02                  BNE   eb1   
E1A6   E6 07                  INC   PLACE+1   
E1A8   A9 57        EB1:      LDA   #"W"   
E1AA   D0 6A                  BNE   ejmp2   ; always
E1AC                             ; A false ( skips: the wrong closer for it is ].
E1AC   A9 5D        SKPAR:    LDA   #"]"   
E1AE   D0 21                  BNE   skip   ; always
E1B0                          ENDIF      
E1B0   20 8A E3     H_DEF:    JSR   getc   
E1B3   38                     SEC      
E1B4   E9 41                  SBC   #"A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
E1B6   A8                     TAY      ;   lands 64 bytes up
E1B7   29 DF                  AND   #0DFh   ; fold case: 0-25 only for a letter
E1B9   C9 1A                  CMP   #26   
E1BB                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BCS   def2   ; not a letter
E1BB                          ENDIF      
E1BB                          IF   CHECKED   
E1BB   B0 E1                  BCS   def1   
E1BD                          ENDIF      
E1BD   98                     TYA      
E1BE   0A                     ASL      
E1BF   A8                     TAY      ; Y -> the cell
E1C0   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E1C2   99 00 04               STA   LET,Y   
E1C5   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E1C7   99 01 04               STA   LET+1,Y   
E1CA   D0 03                  BNE   skdef   ; always: no program is in page zero
E1CC   20 68 E1     DEF2:     JSR   puship   ; an anonymous block: push its address
E1CF                SKDEF:       
E1CF                          IF   CHECKED   
E1CF   A9 29                  LDA   #")"   ; the wrong closer for [
E1D1                          ENDIF      
E1D1                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return it in A.
E1D1                             ; Brackets of both kinds count together; strings are stepped over whole. A
E1D1                             ; NUL first ends the program.
E1D1                             ; In the checked build A holds, on the way in, the wrong closer for the
E1D1                             ; opener that started the skip, kept in T0: ] for (, ) for [, and 0 for \,
E1D1                             ; which takes either. Meeting the wrong closer at this level, or the end
E1D1                             ; (a NUL, or a string that runs into it), stops with N, except for \,
E1D1                             ; which then ends the program as before.
E1D1                SKIP:        
E1D1                          IF   CHECKED   
E1D1   85 04                  STA   T0   
E1D3                          ENDIF      
E1D3   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E1D5   85 09                  STA   D1   ; depth
E1D7   20 8A E3     SK1:      JSR   getc   
E1DA                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BEQ   endprog   
E1DA                          ENDIF      
E1DA                          IF   CHECKED   
E1DA   F0 26                  BEQ   sknul   
E1DC                          ENDIF      
E1DC   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E1DE   D0 05                  BNE   sk2   
E1E0   20 22 E2               JSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h (11h when checked), which
E1E3                             ;   matches nothing below
E1E3                          IF   CHECKED   
E1E3   F0 1D                  BEQ   sknul   ; the string ran into the end
E1E5                          ENDIF      
E1E5   C9 28        SK2:      CMP   #"("   
E1E7   F0 15                  BEQ   sk3   
E1E9   C9 5B                  CMP   #"["   
E1EB   F0 11                  BEQ   sk3   
E1ED   C9 29                  CMP   #")"   
E1EF   F0 04                  BEQ   sk4   
E1F1   C9 5D                  CMP   #"]"   
E1F3   D0 E2                  BNE   sk1   
E1F5   C6 09        SK4:      DEC   D1   
E1F7   10 DE                  BPL   sk1   
E1F9                          IF   CHECKED   
E1F9   C5 04                  CMP   T0   
E1FB   F0 17                  BEQ   e_nest   ; the wrong kind
E1FD                          ENDIF      
E1FD   60                     RTS      ; the closer at this level
E1FE   E6 09        SK3:      INC   D1   
E200   D0 D5                  BNE   sk1   
E202                          IF   CHECKED   
E202   A5 04        SKNUL:    LDA   T0   
E204   D0 0E                  BNE   e_nest   ; ( and [ stop with N
E206   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   ; \ ends the program
E209                             ; The end of "$" (h_print): the string's address goes back into TOS; then a
E209                             ; closing quote drops it, and a NUL (the carry clear) is Q.
E209   68           PQ:       PLA      
E20A   85 02                  STA   TL   
E20C   68                     PLA      
E20D   85 03                  STA   TH   
E20F   B0 57                  BCS   pdrop   
E211   A9 51        E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; a string runs into the end
E213   2C                     DB   2Ch   ; (BIT abs: hides the next instruction)
E214   A9 4E        E_NEST:   LDA   #"N"   ; a skip from ( or [ found the wrong closer
E216   4C E5 E5     EJMP2:    JMP   error   ;   or the end: the place is the opener
E219                          ENDIF      
E219                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
E219   20 68 E1     H_STR:    JSR   puship   
E21C                          IF   CHECKED   
E21C   20 22 E2               JSR   skipstr   
E21F   F0 F0                  BEQ   e_quote   ; it ran into the end: the place is the 22h
E221   60                     RTS      
E222                          ENDIF      
E222                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
E222                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it.
E222                             ; Unchecked, it returns with Z set and A = 22h, and it does not look for the
E222                             ; end. Checked, it returns with Z clear and A = 11h, or with Z set if the
E222                             ; text ended first (a NUL, also one just after "/").
E222                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SKIPSTR:   JSR   getc   
                              CMP   #"/"   
                              BEQ   ss0   
                              CMP   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              RTS      
                    SS0:      JSR   incip   
                              BNE   skipstr   ; A is "/" here
E222                          ENDIF      
E222                          IF   CHECKED   
E222   20 8A E3     SKIPSTR:   JSR   getc   
E225   F0 09                  BEQ   ss9   ; the end
E227   C9 2F                  CMP   #"/"   
E229   D0 06                  BNE   ss1   
E22B   20 8A E3               JSR   getc   ; the escaped character
E22E   D0 F2                  BNE   skipstr   
E230   60           SS9:      RTS      ; the end, just after "/"
E231   C9 22        SS1:      CMP   #22h   
E233   D0 ED                  BNE   skipstr   
E235   4A                     LSR      ; A = 11h, Z clear
E236   60                     RTS      
E237                          ENDIF      
E237                             ; =============================================================================
E237                             ;  Console
E237                             ; =============================================================================
E237                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character from
E237                             ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; "/" plus any other character
E237                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /? is DEL"s "?"; "/" and """ have
E237                             ; no bit 6, so // and /" give themselves). TOS walks along the string; the
E237                             ; checked build keeps the address on the hardware stack meanwhile, for a Q
E237                             ; report (see pq).
E237                          IF   CHECKED   
E237   A5 03        H_PRINT:   LDA   TH   
E239   48                     PHA      
E23A   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E23C   48                     PHA      
E23D   90 03                  BCC   pr0   ; always: the carry is clear on the way in
E23F                          ENDIF      
E23F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   EQU   pr0   
E23F                          ENDIF      
E23F   20 76 E2     PESC0:    JSR   pesc   ; (an escape, and back into the loop)
E242   20 6B E2     PR0:      JSR   tosget   
E245   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E247                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BEQ   pdrop   
E247                          ENDIF      
E247                          IF   CHECKED   
E247   F0 C0                  BEQ   pq   ; the closing quote, with the carry set
E249   A8                     TAY      ; (Y is free here)
E24A   F0 BD                  BEQ   pq   ; a NUL, with the carry clear
E24C                          ENDIF      
E24C   C9 2F                  CMP   #"/"   
E24E   D0 0D                  BNE   pr1   
E250   20 6B E2               JSR   tosget   
E253   C9 60                  CMP   #60h   
E255   90 04                  BCC   pr2   
E257   C9 7F                  CMP   #7Fh   
E259   90 E4                  BCC   pesc0   ; 60h-7Eh, and the carry is clear
E25B   29 BF        PR2:      AND   #0BFh   
E25D   20 03 FF     PR1:      JSR   CONOUT   
E260   4C 42 E2               JMP   pr0   
E263   A5 02        H_EMIT:   LDA   TL   ; "'"
E265   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E268   4C C7 E3     PDROP:    JMP   drop   
E26B                             ; tosget: A = the byte at TOS, and TOS moves on.  inctos: TOS moves on.
E26B   A0 00        TOSGET:   LDY   #0   
E26D   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E26F   E6 02        INCTOS:   INC   TL   
E271   D0 02                  BNE   tg1   
E273   E6 03                  INC   TH   
E275   60           TG1:      RTS      
E276                             ; pesc: the escapes of "$". A = the character after the "/", 60h to 7Eh, and
E276                             ; the carry is clear. Each returns into the loop.
E276                             ;    /a-/z   print the variable, as "#" does
E276                             ;    /{      clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
E276                             ;    /}      clear from the cursor to the end of the line
E276                             ;    /|  /`  show the cursor, hide it
E276                             ;    /~      ( row col addr -- addr ): the cursor to that row and column,
E276                             ;            from 0. The two cells under TOS (the string's address) go.
E276                             ; A - 7Bh sorts them: 00bbIDAsIHwgMSwg 2, ~ 3 with the carry set, and ` E5h, a-z
E276                             ; E6h-FFh with it clear.
E276                          IF   1-ANSI   
E276                             ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's routines do the work.
E276   E9 7A        PESC:     SBC   #7Ah   ; (the carry is clear: - 7Bh)
E278   90 0D                  BCC   pe1   
E27A   F0 08                  BEQ   pcls   ; {
E27C   4A                     LSR      ; | 0, } 1, ~ 1; the carry set for | and ~
E27D   F0 0C                  BEQ   pcur   ; |  show: the carry is set
E27F   B0 0D                  BCS   pat   ; ~
E281   4C 0F FF               JMP   CONEOL   ; }
E284   4C 0C FF     PCLS:     JMP   CONCLS   
E287   C9 E6        PE1:      CMP   #0E6h   
E289   B0 15                  BCS   pvar   
E28B   4C 12 FF     PCUR:     JMP   CONCUR   ; `  hide: the carry is clear
E28E                          ENDIF      
E28E                          IF   ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 1 they are sequences, each a message at MSG (see prs).
                    PESC:     LDY   #M_CLS-MSG   
                              SBC   #7Ah   ; (the carry is clear: - 7Bh)
                              BCC   pe1   
                              BEQ   prs   ; {  ESC [ H ESC [ J
                              LDY   #M_SHOW-MSG   
                              LSR      ; | 0, } 1, ~ 1; the carry set for ~
                              BEQ   prs   ; |  ESC [ ? 2 5 h
                              BCS   pat   ; ~
                              LDY   #M_EOL-MSG   ; }  ESC [ K
                              BNE   prs   ; always
                    PE1:      CMP   #0E6h   
                              BCS   pvar   
                              LDY   #M_HIDE-MSG   ; `  ESC [ ? 2 5 l
                              BNE   prs   ; always
E28E                          ENDIF      
E28E                             ; /~: the column is NOS, the row the cell under it.
E28E                PAT:         
E28E                          IF   CHECKED   
E28E   E0 FA                  CPX   #DSE-2   ; fewer than two cells under TOS: s
E290   B0 0B                  BCS   e_atu   
E292                          ENDIF      
E292                          IF   1-ANSI   
E292   BC 00 02               LDY   DSL,X   ; the column
E295   BD 01 02               LDA   DSL+1,X   ; the row
E298   E8                     INX      
E299   E8                     INX      
E29A   4C 15 FF               JMP   CONAT   
E29D                          ENDIF      
E29D                          IF   ANSI   
                                 ; ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H (ANSI counts from 1). The row's cell and TOS change
                                 ; places first: then "#" prints the row and drops it, prints the column and
                                 ; drops it, and TOS is the string's address again.
                              INX      
                              JSR   h_swap   
                              DEX      
                              LDY   #M_CSI-MSG   
                              JSR   prs   ; ESC [
                              JSR   inctos   
                              JSR   h_num   ; the row + 1
                              LDA   #";"   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              JSR   inctos   
                              JSR   h_num   ; the column + 1
                              LDA   #"H"   
                              JMP   CONOUT   
E29D                          ENDIF      
E29D                          IF   CHECKED   
E29D   4C 68 E0     E_ATU:    JMP   e_stack   ; (X is FAh-FCh: an underflow)
E2A0                          ENDIF      
E2A0                             ; a-z: the carry is set. A + 3Ah is the letter - 41h, as step hands it to
E2A0                             ; lower: that pushes the variable"s address, "@" fetches it, and "#' (next)
E2A0                             ; prints it and drops it: TOS is the string's address again.
E2A0   69 39        PVAR:     ADC   #39h   
E2A2   20 63 E1               JSR   lower   
E2A5   20 43 E5               JSR   h_fetch   
E2A8                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it. The
E2A8                             ; digits are divided off and held on the hardware stack, ended by a 0.
E2A8   A5 03        H_NUM:    LDA   TH   
E2AA   10 08                  BPL   pn1   
E2AC   A9 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
E2AE   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E2B1   20 23 E4               JSR   neg   
E2B4   A9 0A        PN1:      LDA   #10   
E2B6   85 08                  STA   D0   
E2B8   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E2BA   85 09                  STA   D1   
E2BC   48                     PHA      ; the end marker
E2BD   20 0B E5     PN2:      JSR   udiv   
E2C0   A5 04                  LDA   T0   ; the remainder
E2C2   09 30                  ORA   #"0"   
E2C4   48                     PHA      
E2C5   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E2C7   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E2C9   D0 F2                  BNE   pn2   
E2CB   68           PN3:      PLA      
E2CC   F0 9A                  BEQ   pdrop   
E2CE   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E2D1   4C CB E2               JMP   pn3   
E2D4                          IF   CHECKED+ANSI   
E2D4                             ; prs: print the message at MSG+Y; its last byte has bit 7 set. Y ends just
E2D4                             ; past it, at the next message.
E2D4   B9 E2 E2     PRS:      LDA   MSG,Y   
E2D7   48                     PHA      
E2D8   29 7F                  AND   #7Fh   
E2DA   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E2DD   C8                     INY      
E2DE   68                     PLA      
E2DF   10 F3                  BPL   prs   
E2E1   60                     RTS      
E2E2                MSG:         
E2E2                          ENDIF      
E2E2                          IF   ANSI   
                    M_CLS:    DB   27,"[","H",27,"[","J"+80h   
                    M_SHOW:   DB   27,"[","?","2","5","h"+80h   
                    M_HIDE:   DB   27,"[","?","2","5","l"+80h   
                    M_EOL:    DB   27,"[","K"+80h   
                    M_CSI:    DB   27,"["+80h   
E2E2                          ENDIF      
E2E2                          IF   CHECKED   
E2E2   0D 0A 45 72 72 A0 M_ERR:   DB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
E2E8   20 40 A0               DB   " @"," "+80h   
E2EB   0D 8A        M_NL:     DB   13,10+80h   
E2ED   0D 0A 53 74 6B A0 M_STK:   DB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
E2F3   3A 20 2E 2E AE M_CD:   DB   ": ..","."+80h   
E2F8   BA           M_C:      DB   ":"+80h   
E2F9   0D 0A 52 74 6E A0 M_RTN:   DB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
E2FF                          ENDIF      
E2FF                             ; =============================================================================
E2FF                             ;  Dispatch table: one handler per punctuation character, in code order.
E2FF                             ;  Entries are handler-1 for the RTS trick.
E2FF                             ; =============================================================================
E2FF   A7 E3        PTAB:     DW   h_store-1   ; !
E301   18 E2                  DW   h_str-1   ; "
E303   A7 E2                  DW   h_num-1   ; #
E305   36 E2                  DW   h_print-1   ; $
E307   7C E4                  DW   h_swap-1   ; %
E309   D2 E3                  DW   h_and-1   ; &
E30B   62 E2                  DW   h_emit-1   ; '
E30D   81 E1                  DW   h_open-1   ; (
E30F   8E E0                  DW   h_close-1   ; )
E311   55 E4                  DW   h_mul-1   ; *
E313   04 E4                  DW   h_add-1   ; +
E315   4E E5                  DW   h_cfetch-1   ; ,
E317   FC E3                  DW   h_sub-1   ; -
E319   B9 E3                  DW   h_cstore-1   ; .
E31B   91 E4                  DW   h_div-1   ; /
E31D   75 E1                  DW   push-1   ; :
E31F   C6 E3                  DW   drop-1   ; ;
E321   33 E4                  DW   h_lt-1   ; <
E323   45 E4                  DW   h_eq-1   ; =
E325   30 E4                  DW   h_gt-1   ; >
E327   57 E5                  DW   h_key-1   ; ?
E329   42 E5                  DW   h_fetch-1   ; @
E32B   AF E1                  DW   h_def-1   ; [
E32D   A5 E0                  DW   h_break-1   ; \
E32F   94 E0                  DW   h_ret-1   ; ]
E331   EE E3                  DW   h_xor-1   ; ^
E333   C1 E4                  DW   h_alloc-1   ; _
E335   B5 E5                  DW   h_grave-1   ; `
E337   74 E0                  DW   h_tor-1   ; {
E339   E0 E3                  DW   h_or-1   ; |
E33B   81 E0                  DW   h_fromr-1   ; }
E33D   1C E4                  DW   h_not-1   ; ~
E33F                             ; rdnum: TOS = TOS*10 + digit for each digit at IP. Wraps at 16 bits. The
E33F                             ; test is at the bottom so the loop closes with a branch. Returns with the
E33F                             ; carry set.
E33F   20 8D E3     RD1:      JSR   incip   ; (keeps A = the digit)
E342   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E344   26 03                  ROL   TH   ; x2
E346   18                     CLC      
E347   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E349   85 04                  STA   T0   
E34B   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E34D   69 00                  ADC   #0   
E34F   A8                     TAY      ; Y:T0 = x2 + digit
E350   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E352   26 03                  ROL   TH   
E354   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E356   26 03                  ROL   TH   ; x8
E358   18                     CLC      
E359   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E35B   65 04                  ADC   T0   
E35D   85 02                  STA   TL   
E35F   98                     TYA      
E360   65 03                  ADC   TH   
E362   85 03                  STA   TH   ; x8 + x2 + digit
E364   20 6A E3     RDNUM:    JSR   isdig   
E367   90 D6                  BCC   rd1   
E369   60                     RTS      
E36A                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is clear if it is a
E36A                             ; digit. Y = 0.
E36A   20 85 E3     ISDIG:    JSR   peek   
E36D   38                     SEC      
E36E   E9 30                  SBC   #"0"   
E370   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E372   60                     RTS      
E373                             ; =============================================================================
E373                             ;  Reading the program
E373                             ;    peek: A = the character at IP, IP unchanged, Y = 0
E373                             ;    getc: the same, then IP moves on; flags follow A
E373                             ;    incip: IP moves on; keeps A, the carry and Y
E373                             ; =============================================================================
E373                             ; rdhex: if IP is at a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), return its value in A with
E373                             ; the carry clear and IP moved on; otherwise the carry is set and IP stays.
E373                             ; Y = 0.
E373   20 6A E3     RDHEX:    JSR   isdig   
E376   90 0A                  BCC   rh1   
E378   29 DF                  AND   #0DFh   
E37A   E9 11                  SBC   #11h   ; (the carry is set)
E37C   C9 06                  CMP   #6   
E37E   B0 04                  BCS   rh9   
E380   69 0A                  ADC   #10   
E382   90 09        RH1:      BCC   incip   ; always: the carry is clear
E384   60           RH9:      RTS      
E385   A0 00        PEEK:     LDY   #0   
E387   B1 00                  LDA   (IP),Y   
E389   60                     RTS      
E38A   20 85 E3     GETC:     JSR   peek   
E38D   E6 00        INCIP:    INC   IP   
E38F   D0 02                  BNE   ic1   
E391   E6 01                  INC   IP+1   
E393   09 00        IC1:      ORA   #0   
E395   60                     RTS      
E396                             ; rstip: point IP at the start of the program
E396   A9 00        RSTIP:    LDA   #<PROG   
E398   85 00                  STA   IP   
E39A   A9 05                  LDA   #>PROG   
E39C   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E39E   60                     RTS      
E39F                             ; =============================================================================
E39F                             ;  Stack
E39F                             ; =============================================================================
E39F                             ; flag: pops TOS and returns with Z set if it was 0. Keeps the carry.
E39F   A5 02        FLAG:     LDA   TL   
E3A1   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E3A3   20 C7 E3               JSR   drop   
E3A6   A8                     TAY      ; (drop's INX changed the flags)
E3A7   60                     RTS      
E3A8                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." plus the high byte. Both end in drop.
E3A8                H_STORE:      
E3A8                          IF   CHECKED   
E3A8   A5 02                  LDA   TL   ; both bytes must be in the program's space:
E3AA   69 01                  ADC   #1   ; check the page of addr+1 (the carry is
E3AC   A5 03                  LDA   TH   ; clear on the way in)
E3AE   69 00                  ADC   #0   
E3B0   20 02 E5               JSR   chkst   
E3B3                          ENDIF      
E3B3   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E3B6   A0 01                  LDY   #1   
E3B8   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E3BA                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
E3BA                          IF   CHECKED   
E3BA   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E3BC   20 02 E5               JSR   chkst   
E3BF                          ENDIF      
E3BF   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E3C2   A0 00                  LDY   #0   
E3C4   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E3C6   E8                     INX      ; falls into drop
E3C7                             ; drop: ";" and every drop. It works through Y, so A and the carry are kept;
E3C7                             ; it returns with Z clear.
E3C7   BC 00 02     DROP:     LDY   DSL,X   
E3CA   84 02                  STY   TL   
E3CC   BC 00 03               LDY   DSH,X   
E3CF   84 03                  STY   TH   
E3D1   E8                     INX      
E3D2   60                     RTS      
E3D3                             ; =============================================================================
E3D3                             ;  Arithmetic and logic. Effects are ( NOS TOS -- result ).
E3D3                             ; =============================================================================
E3D3                             ; The logic operators leave the carry as they found it, clear, so they can
E3D3                             ; branch to fin.
E3D3   BD 00 02     H_AND:    LDA   DSL,X   
E3D6   25 02                  AND   TL   
E3D8   85 02                  STA   TL   
E3DA   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E3DD   25 03                  AND   TH   
E3DF   90 31                  BCC   fin   ; always
E3E1   BD 00 02     H_OR:     LDA   DSL,X   
E3E4   05 02                  ORA   TL   
E3E6   85 02                  STA   TL   
E3E8   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E3EB   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E3ED   90 23                  BCC   fin   ; always
E3EF   BD 00 02     H_XOR:    LDA   DSL,X   
E3F2   45 02                  EOR   TL   
E3F4   85 02                  STA   TL   
E3F6   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E3F9   45 03                  EOR   TH   
E3FB   90 15                  BCC   fin   ; always
E3FD                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
E3FD   20 6A E3     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
E400   90 14                  BCC   negnum   
E402   20 23 E4     SUB1:     JSR   neg   ; a - b = a + (-b)
E405   18           H_ADD:    CLC      
E406   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E409   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E40B   85 02                  STA   TL   
E40D   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E410   65 03                  ADC   TH   ; falls into fin
E412                             ; fin: finish a two-operand op: A = the high byte of the result
E412   85 03        FIN:      STA   TH   
E414   E8                     INX      
E415   60                     RTS      
E416   A9 00        NEGNUM:   LDA   #0   ; a number from 0 (the digit routine's start)
E418   20 5B E1               JSR   digit   ; (comes back with the carry set)
E41B   B0 06                  BCS   neg   ; always: the number, negated
E41D                             ; "~": -x - 1, which is neg with the carry clear, as it is here
E41D   90 05        H_NOT:    BCC   neg1   ; always
E41F                             ; absv: TOS = |TOS|.  negm: TOS = -TOS if the N flag is set.
E41F   A5 03        ABSV:     LDA   TH   
E421   10 0D        NEGM:     BPL   ab9   
E423                             ; neg: TOS = -TOS
E423   38           NEG:      SEC      
E424   A9 00        NEG1:     LDA   #0   
E426   E5 02                  SBC   TL   
E428   85 02                  STA   TL   
E42A   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E42C   E5 03                  SBC   TH   
E42E   85 03                  STA   TH   
E430   60           AB9:      RTS      
E431                             ; Signed compares: a - b sets N and V; N xor V is "a < b". The carry ends up
E431                             ; clear for true, and bool turns it into -1 (true) or 0 (both pop NOS first).
E431   20 7D E4     H_GT:     JSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
E434   BD 00 02     H_LT:     LDA   DSL,X   
E437   C5 02                  CMP   TL   
E439   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E43C   E5 03                  SBC   TH   
E43E   70 02                  BVS   lt1   
E440   49 80                  EOR   #80h   
E442   0A           LT1:      ASL      
E443   E8                     INX      ; (keeps the carry; never leaves X at 0)
E444   D0 07                  BNE   bool   ; always
E446   20 02 E4     H_EQ:     JSR   sub1   ; a - b: zero if equal; A = its high byte
E449   05 02                  ORA   TL   
E44B   C9 01                  CMP   #1   ; carry clear if A = 0
E44D   A9 00        BOOL:     LDA   #0   
E44F   69 FF                  ADC   #0FFh   ; carry clear: FF, set: 00
E451   85 02                  STA   TL   
E453   85 03                  STA   TH   
E455   60                     RTS      
E456                             ; "*": the classic shift-right multiply. The multiplier leaves TH:TL from the
E456                             ; bottom while the product comes in at the top, through A:T0 above it; after
E456                             ; 16 rounds TH:TL hold the low 16 bits, which are all that is kept.
E456   A0 10        H_MUL:    LDY   #16   ; the round count
E458   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E45A   85 04                  STA   T0   ; A:T0 = the upper half
E45C   46 03                  LSR   TH   
E45E   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; the first multiplier bit
E460   90 0F        ML1:      BCC   ml2   
E462   85 05                  STA   T1   
E464   18                     CLC      
E465   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E467   7D 00 02               ADC   DSL,X   
E46A   85 04                  STA   T0   
E46C   A5 05                  LDA   T1   
E46E   7D 00 03               ADC   DSH,X   ; upper half += the multiplicand
E471   6A           ML2:      ROR      
E472   66 04                  ROR   T0   
E474   66 03                  ROR   TH   
E476   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; everything one place right; next bit out
E478   88                     DEY      
E479   D0 E5                  BNE   ml1   
E47B   E8                     INX      ; drop the multiplicand
E47C   60                     RTS      
E47D   BC 00 02     H_SWAP:   LDY   DSL,X   ; "%"
E480   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E482   9D 00 02               STA   DSL,X   
E485   84 02                  STY   TL   
E487   BC 00 03               LDY   DSH,X   
E48A   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E48C   9D 00 03               STA   DSH,X   
E48F   84 03                  STY   TH   
E491   60                     RTS      
E492                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
E492                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b, r is pushed
E492                             ; and gets the sign of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no
E492                             ; meaning; checked, it stops with Z.
E492                H_DIV:       
E492                          IF   CHECKED   
E492   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E494   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E496   F0 5F                  BEQ   e_zero   
E498                          ENDIF      
E498   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E49B   48                     PHA      ; a's sign: for r
E49C   45 03                  EOR   TH   
E49E   48                     PHA      ; a xor b: for q
E49F   20 1F E4               JSR   absv   
E4A2   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E4A4   85 08                  STA   D0   
E4A6   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E4A8   85 09                  STA   D1   ; D = |b|
E4AA   20 C7 E3               JSR   drop   ; TOS = a
E4AD   20 1F E4               JSR   absv   ; TOS = |a|
E4B0   20 0B E5               JSR   udiv   ; TOS = q, T0/T1 = r
E4B3   68                     PLA      
E4B4   20 21 E4               JSR   negm   ; q's sign
E4B7   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E4B9   A4 05                  LDY   T1   
E4BB   20 6C E1               JSR   pushay   ; r on top
E4BE   68                     PLA      
E4BF   4C 21 E4               JMP   negm   ; r's sign
E4C2                             ; =============================================================================
E4C2                             ;  Storage
E4C2                             ; =============================================================================
E4C2                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap top moves by n, which is signed: a negative
E4C2                             ; count releases. TOS becomes the old top. (The carry is clear on the way in.)
E4C2                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_ALLOC:   LDA   HEAP   
                              TAY      
                              ADC   TL   
                              STA   HEAP   
                              STY   TL   
                              LDA   HEAP+1   
                              TAY      
                              ADC   TH   
                              STA   HEAP+1   
                              STY   TH   
                              RTS      
E4C2                          ENDIF      
E4C2                             ; The checked build works the new top out first, in T0 and Y, and stops with
E4C2                             ; H, the count still on the stack, if it is at or past the limit, below the
E4C2                             ; program's end, or if the 16-bit add wrapped. A wrap is the V flag of the
E4C2                             ; high bytes" add with the old top"s sign bit flipped: that makes the old top
E4C2                             ; a signed number from -8000h, so the add overflows exactly when the true
E4C2                             ; sum leaves 0000h-FFFFh.
E4C2                          IF   CHECKED   
E4C2   AD 7C 04     H_ALLOC:   LDA   HEAP   
E4C5   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E4C7   85 04                  STA   T0   
E4C9   AD 7D 04               LDA   HEAP+1   
E4CC   49 80                  EOR   #80h   
E4CE   65 03                  ADC   TH   
E4D0   70 28                  BVS   e_heap   ; wrapped
E4D2   49 80                  EOR   #80h   ; the new top's high byte
E4D4   C9 E0                  CMP   #HEAPLIM   
E4D6   B0 22                  BCS   e_heap   ; at or past the limit
E4D8   A8                     TAY      
E4D9   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E4DB   CD 38 04               CMP   PEND   
E4DE   98                     TYA      
E4DF   ED 39 04               SBC   PEND+1   
E4E2   90 16                  BCC   e_heap   ; below the program's end
E4E4   AD 7C 04               LDA   HEAP   
E4E7   85 02                  STA   TL   
E4E9   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E4EB   8D 7C 04               STA   HEAP   
E4EE   AD 7D 04               LDA   HEAP+1   
E4F1   85 03                  STA   TH   
E4F3   8C 7D 04               STY   HEAP+1   
E4F6   60                     RTS      
E4F7                             ; Errors found by handlers. The stacks are as they were before the handler.
E4F7   A9 5A        E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; divide by zero
E4F9   2C                     DB   2Ch   ; (BIT abs: hides the next instruction)
E4FA   A9 48        E_HEAP:   LDA   #"H"   ; heap past the limit or below the program
E4FC   2C                     DB   2Ch   
E4FD   A9 4F        E_STORE:   LDA   #"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
E4FF   4C E5 E5               JMP   error   
E502                             ; chkst: stop unless the page in A is in the program's own space, from the
E502                             ; letter page up to the heap limit. Keeps Y.
E502   C9 04        CHKST:    CMP   #LETPAGE   
E504   90 F7                  BCC   e_store   
E506   C9 E0                  CMP   #HEAPLIM   
E508   B0 F3                  BCS   e_store   
E50A   60                     RTS      
E50B                          ENDIF      
E50B                             ; udiv: unsigned TOS / D (D <= 8000h). TOS becomes the quotient and T0/T1
E50B                             ; the remainder. The low byte of each trial subtraction waits on the
E50B                             ; hardware stack.
E50B                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
E50B   A9 00        UDIV:     LDA   #0   
E50D   85 04                  STA   T0   
E50F   85 05                  STA   T1   
E511   A5 08                  LDA   D0   
E513   49 02                  EOR   #2   
E515   05 09                  ORA   D1   
E517   D0 07                  BNE   ud0   
E519   46 03                  LSR   TH   
E51B   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; the quotient
E51D   26 04                  ROL   T0   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
E51F   60                     RTS      
E520   A0 10        UD0:      LDY   #16   
E522   06 02        UD1:      ASL   TL   
E524   26 03                  ROL   TH   
E526   26 04                  ROL   T0   
E528   26 05                  ROL   T1   
E52A   38                     SEC      
E52B   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E52D   E5 08                  SBC   D0   
E52F   48                     PHA      
E530   A5 05                  LDA   T1   
E532   E5 09                  SBC   D1   
E534   90 08                  BCC   ud2   
E536   85 05                  STA   T1   
E538   68                     PLA      
E539   85 04                  STA   T0   
E53B   E6 02                  INC   TL   ; the quotient bit (TL's bit 0 is free)
E53D   24                     DB   24h   ; (BIT zp: steps over the PLA)
E53E   68           UD2:      PLA      
E53F   88                     DEY      
E540   D0 E0                  BNE   ud1   
E542   60                     RTS      
E543                             ; =============================================================================
E543                             ;  Console
E543                             ; =============================================================================
E543   A0 01        H_FETCH:   LDY   #1   ; "@"
E545   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E547   48                     PHA      ; the high byte, while "," gets the low one
E548   20 4F E5               JSR   h_cfetch   
E54B   68                     PLA      
E54C   85 03                  STA   TH   
E54E   60                     RTS      
E54F                H_CFETCH:      ; ","
E54F   A0 00                  LDY   #0   
E551   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E553   85 02        CF2:      STA   TL   ; TOS = A (low), Y (high)
E555   84 03                  STY   TH   
E557   60                     RTS      
E558                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
E558                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
E558                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
E558                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
E558                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
E558   A5 03        H_KEY:    LDA   TH   
E55A   30 20                  BMI   line   
E55C   A0 28        KT1:      LDY   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
E55E   20 BA E0     KT2:      JSR   getk   
E561   D0 15                  BNE   kt3   
E563   88                     DEY      
E564   D0 F8                  BNE   kt2   
E566   A5 02                  LDA   TL   ; count the millisecond off:
E568   D0 06                  BNE   kt4   
E56A   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E56C   F0 EE                  BEQ   kt1   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
E56E   C6 03                  DEC   TH   
E570   C6 02        KT4:      DEC   TL   
E572   D0 E8                  BNE   kt1   
E574   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E576   D0 E4                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
E578   A0 00        KT3:      LDY   #0   
E57A   F0 D7                  BEQ   cf2   ; always: TOS = A
E57C                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
E57C                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
E57C                             ; is full. Y = the length so far; TL = the most allowed.
E57C   20 23 E4     LINE:     JSR   neg   ; TOS = the count, and A = its high byte
E57F   D0 04                  BNE   ln0   
E581   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E583   10 04                  BPL   ln1   
E585   A9 7F        LN0:      LDA   #127   ; more than 127 is taken as 127
E587   85 02                  STA   TL   
E589   A0 00        LN1:      LDY   #0   
E58B   F0 03                  BEQ   ln2   ; always
E58D   20 03 FF     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
E590   20 BA E0     LN2:      JSR   getk   
E593   F0 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
E595   C9 0D                  CMP   #13   
E597   F0 14                  BEQ   ln5   
E599   C9 08                  CMP   #8   
E59B   F0 0A                  BEQ   ln4   
E59D   C4 02                  CPY   TL   
E59F   B0 EF                  BCS   ln2   ; full
E5A1   99 80 04               STA   LINEBUF,Y   
E5A4   C8                     INY      
E5A5   D0 E6                  BNE   ln3   ; always: echo it
E5A7   88           LN4:      DEY      ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
E5A8   10 E3                  BPL   ln3   
E5AA   C8                     INY      ;   unless the line was empty
E5AB   F0 E3                  BEQ   ln2   ; always
E5AD   99 80 04     LN5:      STA   LINEBUF,Y   ; A = CR
E5B0   A9 80                  LDA   #<LINEBUF   
E5B2   A0 04                  LDY   #>LINEBUF   
E5B4   D0 9D                  BNE   cf2   ; always: TOS = the line's address
E5B6                             ; =============================================================================
E5B6                             ;  Machine code: the grave
E5B6                             ; =============================================================================
E5B6                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
E5B6                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (60h) is
E5B6                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
E5B6                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ); see the
E5B6                             ; contract in the header.
E5B6   20 73 E3     H_GRAVE:   JSR   rdhex   
E5B9   B0 1C                  BCS   exec   
E5BB   0A           HX1:      ASL      
E5BC   0A                     ASL      
E5BD   0A                     ASL      
E5BE   0A                     ASL      
E5BF   85 04                  STA   T0   
E5C1   20 73 E3               JSR   rdhex   
E5C4   B0 0C                  BCS   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
E5C6   05 04                  ORA   T0   
E5C8   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   ; Y is 0 after rdhex (never checked)
E5CA   20 6F E2               JSR   inctos   
E5CD   20 73 E3               JSR   rdhex   
E5D0   90 E9                  BCC   hx1   
E5D2   A9 60        HX2:      LDA   #60h   
E5D4   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E5D6   60                     RTS      
E5D7   A5 02        EXEC:     LDA   TL   
E5D9   85 04                  STA   T0   
E5DB   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E5DD   85 05                  STA   T1   
E5DF   20 C7 E3               JSR   drop   ; the address is consumed
E5E2   6C 04 00               JMP   (T0)   
E5E5                          IF   CHECKED   
E5E5                             ; =============================================================================
E5E5                             ;  Checked build: the error report
E5E5                             ; =============================================================================
E5E5                             ; error: the report, then EXIT. A = the letter, PLACE = the place, X = the
E5E5                             ; data stack to show, RSV = S for the Rtn line. Nothing here relies on S: an
E5E5                             ; overflowed or underflowed hardware stack wraps inside its page, and only
E5E5                             ; its depth is shown.
E5E5                             ;   CR LF
E5E5                             ;   Err X @ line,col CR LF
E5E5                             ;   up to 16 characters from the place, raw, up to a CR, LF or NUL  CR LF
E5E5                             ;   Stk n: [...] and the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top  CR LF
E5E5                             ;   Rtn n CR LF
E5E5                             ; The numbers go through "#" (prnum), which pushes them over the data stack
E5E5                             ; and pops them again, so the stack is shown as it was.
E5E5   48           ERROR:    PHA      ; the letter
E5E6   A0 00                  LDY   #M_ERR-MSG   
E5E8   20 D4 E2               JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Err "
E5EB   68                     PLA      
E5EC   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E5EF   20 D4 E2               JSR   prs   ; " @ " (it follows M_ERR)
E5F2   20 82 E6               JSR   lcol   
E5F5   A5 08                  LDA   D0   
E5F7   A4 09                  LDY   D1   
E5F9   20 7C E6               JSR   prnum   ; the line
E5FC   A9 2C                  LDA   #","   
E5FE   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E601   A5 0A                  LDA   CL   
E603   A4 0B                  LDY   CL+1   
E605   20 7C E6               JSR   prnum   ; the column
E608   A0 09                  LDY   #M_NL-MSG   
E60A   20 D4 E2               JSR   prs   
E60D   A0 00                  LDY   #0   ; the text at the place
E60F   B1 06        ER1:      LDA   (PLACE),Y   
E611   F0 10                  BEQ   er2   
E613   C9 0D                  CMP   #13   
E615   F0 0C                  BEQ   er2   
E617   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E619   F0 08                  BEQ   er2   
E61B   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E61E   C8                     INY      
E61F   C0 10                  CPY   #16   
E621   D0 EC                  BNE   er1   
E623   A0 0B        ER2:      LDY   #M_STK-MSG   
E625   20 D4 E2               JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Stk "
E628   8A                     TXA      
E629   49 FF                  EOR   #0FFh   
E62B   38                     SEC      
E62C   E9 03                  SBC   #0FFh-DSE   ; the depth, DSE - X (FFh, an overflow: 253)
E62E   48                     PHA      
E62F   20 7A E6               JSR   prnum8   
E632   68                     PLA      
E633   A0 16                  LDY   #M_C-MSG   ; ":"
E635   C9 09                  CMP   #9   
E637   90 04                  BCC   er3   
E639   A9 08                  LDA   #8   ; more than 8: ": ..." and the top 8
E63B   A0 11                  LDY   #M_CD-MSG   
E63D   85 06        ER3:      STA   T2   ; T2 = how many cells to show (the place
E63F                             ;   is no longer needed)
E63F   20 D4 E2               JSR   prs   
E642   20 76 E1               JSR   push   ; TOS into memory with the rest: cell i from
E645                             ;   the top is at DSL+X+i now
E645   A5 06        ER4:      LDA   T2   ; cells T2-1 down to 0, the top last
E647   F0 1B                  BEQ   er5   
E649   C6 06                  DEC   T2   
E64B   A9 20                  LDA   #" "   
E64D   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E650   8A                     TXA      
E651   18                     CLC      
E652   65 06                  ADC   T2   
E654   A8                     TAY      
E655   B9 00 02               LDA   DSL,Y   
E658   48                     PHA      
E659   B9 00 03               LDA   DSH,Y   
E65C   A8                     TAY      
E65D   68                     PLA      
E65E   20 7C E6               JSR   prnum   
E661   4C 45 E6               JMP   er4   
E664   A0 17        ER5:      LDY   #M_RTN-MSG   
E666   20 D4 E2               JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Rtn "
E669   AD 35 04               LDA   RSV   
E66C   49 FF                  EOR   #0FFh   
E66E   4A                     LSR      ; (FFh - S) / 2 entries
E66F   20 7A E6               JSR   prnum8   
E672   A0 09                  LDY   #M_NL-MSG   
E674   20 D4 E2               JSR   prs   
E677   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   
E67A                             ; prnum: print the number A (low), Y (high), signed, keeping the data stack.
E67A                             ; prnum8: the same for A alone, 0-255.
E67A   A0 00        PRNUM8:   LDY   #0   
E67C   20 6C E1     PRNUM:    JSR   pushay   
E67F   4C A8 E2               JMP   h_num   
E682                             ; lcol: the line (D0/D1) and the column (CL) of the place, both from 1. A
E682                             ; place below the program is in the -n? line buffer: line 0, and the column
E682                             ; is the place in the buffer. Otherwise IP (free now: the program has
E682                             ; stopped) runs from PROG to the place, counting LFs; CL keeps where the
E682                             ; last line started, and the column is the place minus that, plus 1.
E682   A9 00        LCOL:     LDA   #0   
E684   85 09                  STA   D1   
E686   85 08                  STA   D0   
E688   A9 80                  LDA   #<LINEBUF   
E68A   85 0A                  STA   CL   
E68C   A9 04                  LDA   #>LINEBUF   
E68E   85 0B                  STA   CL+1   
E690   A5 06                  LDA   PLACE   
E692   C9 00                  CMP   #<PROG   
E694   A5 07                  LDA   PLACE+1   
E696   E9 05                  SBC   #>PROG   
E698   90 26                  BCC   lc9   ; below the program: line 0
E69A   E6 08                  INC   D0   
E69C   20 96 E3               JSR   rstip   
E69F   A5 00        LC3:      LDA   IP   ; a line starts here
E6A1   85 0A                  STA   CL   
E6A3   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E6A5   85 0B                  STA   CL+1   
E6A7   A5 00        LC1:      LDA   IP   
E6A9   C5 06                  CMP   PLACE   
E6AB   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E6AD   E5 07                  SBC   PLACE+1   
E6AF   B0 0F                  BCS   lc9   ; at the place
E6B1   20 8A E3               JSR   getc   
E6B4   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E6B6   D0 EF                  BNE   lc1   
E6B8   E6 08                  INC   D0   ; an LF: a new line starts after it
E6BA   D0 E3                  BNE   lc3   
E6BC   E6 09                  INC   D1   
E6BE   D0 DF                  BNE   lc3   ; always
E6C0   A5 06        LC9:      LDA   PLACE   
E6C2   38                     SEC      
E6C3   E5 0A                  SBC   CL   
E6C5   85 0A                  STA   CL   
E6C7   A5 07                  LDA   PLACE+1   
E6C9   E5 0B                  SBC   CL+1   
E6CB   85 0B                  STA   CL+1   
E6CD   E6 0A                  INC   CL   ; + 1
E6CF   D0 02                  BNE   lc8   
E6D1   E6 0B                  INC   CL+1   
E6D3   60           LC8:      RTS      
E6D4                          ENDIF      


